{"id": "1545591626892574810", "channel_id": "1544152565921611837", "author_id": "299849115439857664", "author_name": "kevin7907", "content": "My suggestions for the sake of the future:\n1. It doesn’t matter if it is only for super whales but AA carries with proper supports should have viable damage to clear madness. The numbers should be adjusted to match. This will make people want to spend.\n2. There’s no reason to limit the dtide to 4 difficulties. With the new adjustments there is now a big gap from hard to nightmare difficulty.", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T00:29:19.555000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544152565921611837", "thread_title": "D-tide Feedback (New)", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542479601241030726"]}
{"id": "1545595804805369967", "channel_id": "1544152565921611837", "author_id": "485874572390826013", "author_name": "catuniverse", "content": "I'm a 2-month player who spent a small amount before the d-tide update (got enough silver to activate premium archive rewards) and have just finished Arc 2 Chapter 3 Normal and Arc 1 Chapter 7 Hard with full achievements/silver.\n\nFor a new person like me there are lots of charming characters and a lot of story, but also so many adjustments and multiple wildly different gameplay rules to adjust to. I got good at Legacy mode, now need to learn Astral mode with no in-game hand-holding. I got good at classic Realms, now Divine realms function very differently (especially Caro and Ultra compared to the original style).\n\nI just got into high ranks (like the top 1600) on P-Dive and only completed D-tide once, just before this update, not getting a high score but just trying to learn how it all works as a new person. \n\nI think the devs (or publishers, whoever is pressuring all these rapid changes) have underestimated how many hurdles they are creating with so many radical gameplay changes for players, especially new folks who were willing to spend and learn a lot of these changing rules already. JP server realm experimentation already feels like a mistake. It doubles the work for devs (for now, while 2 different rulesets are active at once) and requires a heavy hand to lead your players to new characters when they often prefer the old style. Now even more heavy-handedness with game modes that were praised before.\n\nOf note, existing player guides for newbies (and there's only really 2 of these due to a small community) only coach people through the old D-tide. As a new player who studied that and just got to try it once: I'm absolutely not learning a new, harder D-tide now. Why would I? For fun? It's not fun. It's not encouraging people to spend, it encourages new people to ignore D-tide entirely.", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T00:45:55.647000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544152565921611837", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 9}], "thread_title": "D-tide Feedback (New)", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542479601241030726"]}
